  "body": "Please, add a css property on a block for auto scroll when drag pointer into content like as mobile but in desktop. By example:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<div style=\"height: 2000px; overflow-y: scroll; drag-with: $value\"></div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen `$value` can: `mouse-wheel`, `pointer-drag`, `touch` (by default), `any` or `none`. With `none` value can not scroll the content with the finger on mobile or native mouse scroll, only from javscript, useful for simulate console or progress contents.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, please, add a css property to set the auto scroll to bottom when modify content or from dom. This avoids having to simulate scrolling from javascript when adding content and should always show the last item down. By example:\r\n\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<div style=\"height: 2000px; overflow-y: scroll; scroll-to-bottom: $event\"></div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen event can `none` (by default), `change-content` (forced), `visible-change-content`. When `visible-change-content` apply only when add a new content and user is in bottom of content, when user need scroll to top, the event can not effect.\r\n\r\nI know this is just an idea that should be improved, but it is a necessity that is repeated in many styles and designs and it must be done manually using calculations of scroll positions v / s content height that are not always very exact values and the Javascript simulation is very slow on desktop, it would be better if the browser render engine takes care of this so that the movement is more fluid and the user experience is better. ",
